Creative Editor & Brand Asset Management Platform
Product Architecture & Engineering Blueprint
Executive Overview
This specification outlines the technical architecture, domain data structures, backoffice systems, and implementation sequence for a cloud-native, multi-tenant creative composition engine. The platform is engineered to serve two distinct operational models:

Consumer / B2C Workflows: Frictionless, form-driven generation of personal stationary, event collateral, and invitations powered by a constrained 3-layer canvas and an automated layout engine.
Enterprise / B2B Workflows: Workspace-isolated brand repositories, governance engines with fine-grained layer-locking capabilities, corporate typography enforcement, and automated multi-format ad set rendering.
Core Modules & Functional Architecture
Three-Layer Canvas Layout Engine
To prevent z-index drift and ensure layout consistency across varying screen viewports, the canvas engine enforces an explicit three-layer stratification:

Layer Level
Layer Designation
Responsibilities & Capabilities
Locking & Constraints
Layer 1
Background Layer
Solid fills, linear/radial gradients, repetitive pattern fills, textures, or full-bleed photography.
Isolated from pointer events by default; z-index strictly fixed at lowest stack index.
Layer 2
Content & Typography Layer
Pre-configured typography pairings (Display Header, Subtitle, Body), dynamic form variables, geometric vector dividers, and contextual text containers.
Supports smart grouping, automatic vertical flow wrapping, and bounded text manipulation.
Layer 3
Assets & Dynamic Overlays
Vector badges, contextual thematic stickers, dynamic photo frame masks, decorative ribbons, and custom user overlays.
Free-floating or pinned relative to Layer 2 text bounding boxes with multi-touch transform handles.

Thematic Generator Pipeline
Structured Form Inputs: Captures core event parameters including categorical taxonomy (e.g., Wedding, Corporate Gala, Birthday), target emotional tone, color palette restrictions, and schedule metadata.
Automated Batch Processing: Transposes tabular schedule and host metadata across complete collateral suites (invitations, schedules, directional signage, name tags) while maintaining unified typography and palette styles.
Generative Expansion: Integrates multimodal AI pipelines (GPT-4o for contextual copy tailoring; Stability AI / DALL-E 3 for bespoke vector/raster sticker generations).
Enterprise Governance & Multi-Tenancy
Workspaces & Brand Kits: Isolated storage partitioning for client-approved vector marks, strict hex color ramps, web fonts, and composition guides.
Administrative Governance Engine: Fine-grained locking rules allowing template authors to freeze coordinate positions, dimensions, rotation, or content values on a per-element basis.
Automated Creative Sets: Parallel rasterization engine producing responsive aspect ratios (1:1, 9:16, 16:9, 4:5) from a single master layout configuration.
