Entity Specifications
users: Manages entity credentials, session tokens, and contextual permission scopes (platform_admin, workspace_manager, creative_editor, consumer).
companies: Top-level multi-tenant domain boundary encapsulating seat allocations, subscription tiers, and storage quotas.
brand_kits: Defines scoped visual boundaries—custom typography stacks, primary/secondary palettes, and master vector assets.
templates: Serialized Konva scene trees defining root canvas bounds, layer order, default asset placements, and individual node locking rules.
creatives: Instance representations containing template diffs, text overrides, localized image frames, and output render history.
assets: Catalog entries for raw system vectors, curated backgrounds, licensed typography (.woff2), and user-uploaded media.
billing_subscriptions: Tracks Stripe customer references, active entitlements, prepaid rendering credits, and monthly creative batch allowances.
Backoffice Administration Engine
The internal operational dashboard provides systems administrators and content creators with foundational control over platform primitives:

Global Asset Catalog: Bulk ingestion pipeline with automated vector sanitization, metadata tagging, and aspect-ratio normalization.
Typography Engine: Licensing verification, automated WOFF/WOFF2 webfont conversion, unicode range subsetting, and line-height metric testing.
Preset Grouping Builder: Interactive staging canvas allowing design teams to assemble, balance, and save multi-element typography and embellishment groups.
Template & Lock Inspector: Administrative staging environment enabling granular state flags on all canvas nodes:
allowContentEdit: Permit string or source image manipulation.
allowTransform: Permit resizing, rotating, or repositioning.
allowDelete: Permit node deletion from the visual stack.
AI Smart Search & Asset Metadata Engine
To power semantic, intent-based search for users (e.g., matching a prompt like "elegant vintage floral wedding invitation" to appropriate backgrounds, text groups, and stickers), all catalog items store rich structured metadata.
1. Asset Metadata Schema Extensions
Background Metadata: Visual taxonomy (color palette, gradient type, texture style), mood/tone (elegant, playful, formal, rustic), occasion tags (wedding, birthday, corporate), and orientation/aspect ratio support.
Text Group Metadata: Layout archetype (centered stack, left-aligned minimal, split header), formality rating, typography style pairing (serif display + sans body), target occasion, and replaceable variable slots ({{event_name}}, {{date}}, {{host_name}}).
Sticker & Overlay Metadata: Graphic style (flat vector, watercolor, 3D render, line art), theme taxonomy, primary/secondary colors, and bounding box snap constraints.
2. Vector Embeddings & Hybrid Search Architecture
Vector Store: PostgreSQL with pgvector extension (or dedicated vector databases like Qdrant/Pinecone).
Embedding Model: Text and image embedding generation using OpenAI text-embedding-3-large or CLIP models for multi-modal matching (text prompt to image asset).
Hybrid Search Strategy: Combines dense vector similarity (semantic meaning) with sparse metadata filtering (exact occasion/color/aspect ratio matches).
3. AI Smart Composition Pipeline
User inputs natural language request or selects occasion attributes.
LLM extracts target style, color preferences, and required template variables.
Hybrid search retrieves top-ranked candidate backgrounds, complementary text groups, and accent stickers.
Layout engine automatically composes candidate 3-layer preview cards for user selection.
Implementation Roadmap
Phase 1: Core Canvas Engine & State Architecture
Initialize Next.js project with Konva scene-graph implementation.
Construct the 3-layer isolation pipeline with drag-and-drop, aspect-constrained transforms, and history management (undo/redo).
Implement serialization/deserialization to export and import canvas layouts via standard JSON payloads.
Phase 2: Administrative Tooling & Asset Repositories
Develop backoffice UI for typography ingestion, vector categorization, and preset group creation.
Configure AWS S3 media ingestion pipelines with automatic image optimization and CDN delivery.
Deploy PostgreSQL schema using Prisma ORM with baseline multi-tenant permission isolation.
Phase 3: Thematic Generator & Generative Integration
Implement the dynamic event generation form capturing schedule, color, and motif constraints.
Connect the generation pipeline to GPT-4o for dynamic copy-fitting and Stability AI for custom asset synthesis.
Build automated batch-rendering routines for multi-asset collateral sets.
Phase 4: Enterprise Workspace Isolation & Monetization
Deploy granular node-locking enforcement inside the editor view for non-admin roles.
Introduce multi-tenant workspace routing, brand kit validation, and team permission checks.
Integrate Stripe Billing to support metered consumer micro-transactions and automated enterprise SaaS subscriptions.

